From da5afe3c72d736a9b7bf6fbf961cef50639c8984 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: a lock of the clocks that a crash left is let go on
 the thread of the hold

CActiveAESink::Start() runs on the thread of the audio engine, before the
loop of that thread, and the start of Kodi waits up to 10 s for the engine to
answer INIT (CActiveAE::Start()). Where the marker of a lock that a crash left
was there, RecoverStale() loaded NVML, initialised it and reset the clocks
right there: nvmlInit() can take a second or more with the GPU asleep, and a
driver that does not answer kept the whole audio engine from starting, which
GpuClockHold.h says never happens ("never makes the audio engine wait").

Start() now only reads the marker (one file, normally absent) and, where it
is there, hands it to the hold (CAsyncHold::Recover()), whose thread lets that
lock go before anything that is asked after it: a stream of HD audio played at
once on the same card is locked after the reset, not reset by it.

TestGpuClockHold: AStaleLockIsLetGoOnTheThreadOfTheHoldFirst (Recover()
returns at once with a driver that takes 300 ms to answer, and the stale lock
is let go before the new one is made) and NoMarkerNoRecovery. A copy of the
header that lets go on the thread that asks fails the first; one that lets go
after the requests hangs. The 13 tests pass.
